<%- include('partials/head') %>
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="site-wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Guide for families</p>
    <h1>IB Diploma or A Level?</h1>
    <p class="lead">Both are respected pre-university qualifications. They suit different students, so here is how they compare.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<div class="site-wrap">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="table-wrap panel">
      <table class="table compare">
        <thead><tr><th></th><th>IB Diploma Programme</th><th>A Level</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Subjects</th><td>Six subjects from different groups (a language, sciences, maths, humanities and more): usually three at Higher Level and three at Standard Level</td><td>Usually three or four subjects of the student’s choice, with no required mix</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Core</th><td>Theory of Knowledge, a 4,000-word Extended Essay, and Creativity, Activity, Service (CAS)</td><td>No compulsory core</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Assessment</th><td>Final exams plus Internal Assessments in each subject</td><td>Mostly final exams, with coursework in some subjects</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Grading</th><td>Points out of 45 (up to 7 per subject, plus up to 3 from the core)</td><td>A* to E for each subject</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Strength</th><td>Breadth, independent inquiry and a global outlook</td><td>Depth in a few chosen subjects</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-2">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>The IB Diploma may suit students who…</h3>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>enjoy many subjects and don’t want to drop languages, sciences or humanities yet</li>
        <li>are still deciding what to study at university</li>
        <li>are organised and can manage long-term work such as the Extended Essay and IAs</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>A Levels may suit students who…</h3>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>already know which subjects they want to study at university</li>
        <li>want to go deep in a few subjects, such as maths and the sciences</li>
        <li>do their best work in final exams</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <p>Neither route is “better”. Universities around the world accept both. What matters most is a good school, a good fit for the student, and steady support along the way. Our tutors teach both <a href="/ib-tuition">IB</a> and <a href="/cambridge-tuition">Cambridge A Level</a> students, and we are happy to talk it through with you.</p>
    <h3>Further reading</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.timeshighereducation.com/student/news/international-baccalaureate-versus-a-levels" rel="noopener" target="_blank">The International Baccalaureate versus A levels</a> (Times Higher Education)</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.telegraph.co.uk/education/educationadvice/11994093/IB-vs-A-levels-how-my-family-put-both-to-the-test.html" rel="noopener" target="_blank">IB vs A-levels: how my family put both to the test</a> (The Telegraph)</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.ibo.org/programmes/diploma-programme/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">IB Diploma Programme</a> (International Baccalaureate)</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.cambridgeinternational.org/programmes-and-qualifications/cambridge-advanced/cambridge-international-as-and-a-levels/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Cambridge International AS &amp; A Levels</a> (Cambridge International)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <%- include('partials/cta') %>
</div>
